N:;;;;
FN:No Name Restaurant
ORG:No Name Restaurant;
TEL;type=WORK;type=VOICE;type=pref:617-338-7539
ADR;type=HOME;type=pref:;;15 Fish Pier St W;Boston;MA;02210;United States of America
NOTE:Seafood\nCheap\nKids\n\nFrom http://www.evite.com/pages/venue/venueDetails.jsp?venueID=MEMDLAFFNXIQOGHLFATP:\n\nHours\nMon-Sat 11am-10pm\nSun 11am-9pm \n\n\nIn Short\nThe No Name's large dining room sports a no-frills feel\, and prices are kept low\, in part\, due to the lack of linen napkins or tablecloths. Congenial waiters recommend their favorites off the limited menu. The fish is as fresh as it gets\, and all the kitchen does is either fry it or bake it. Popular choices include baked scrod\, fried calamari and shrimp scampi. Dessert options include straightforward fruit pies and grapenut pudding.\nInsider Tips\nKeep an eye on the neighboring Bank of America Pavillion's concert schedule--the area is a mess on event nights.\n\nSeafood\nCheap\nKids\n\nFrom http://www.evite.com/pages/venue/venueDetails.jsp?venueID=MEMDLAFFNXIQOGHLFATP:\n\nHours\nMon-Sat 11am-10pm\nSun 11am-9pm \n\n\nIn Short\nThe No Name's large dining room sports a no-frills feel\n\, and prices are kept low\, in part\, due to the lack of linen napkins or tablecloths. Congenial waiters recommend their favorites off the limited menu. The fish is as fresh as it gets\, and all the kitchen does is either fry it or bake it. Popular choices include baked scrod\, fried calamari and shrimp scampi. Dessert options include straightforward fruit pies and grapenut pudding.\nInsider Tips\nKeep an eye on the neighboring Bank of America Pavillion's concert schedule--the area is a mess on event nights.\n
X-ABShowAs:COMPANY
END:VCARD
